  <main class="container">
    <div class="eyebrow">Negative Equity Car Loan Calculator</div>

    <h1>Negative Equity Car Loan Calculator</h1>

    <p class="intro">
      Owe more on your car than it is worth? This calculator shows the negative-equity
      gap, how much old debt would roll into the next auto loan, the estimated new payment,
      and the resulting loan-to-value. It also checks whether cash down actually fixes the
      problem or simply leaves the household with less emergency savings.
    </p>

    <p class="intro">
      Use it before accepting a trade-in offer, stretching a loan to 72 or 84 months, or
      assuming a dealer can make an underwater balance disappear. The old debt has to be
      paid somewhere: with cash, a higher new loan, a higher-priced deal, or more time.
    </p>

    <div class="calculator">
      <div class="calc-grid">
        <div class="calc-field">
          <label for="currentPayoff">Current Loan Payoff ($)</label>
          <input type="number" id="currentPayoff" placeholder="24000" min="0" inputmode="decimal" />
        </div>

        <div class="calc-field">
          <label for="tradeValue">Trade-In or Sale Value ($)</label>
          <input type="number" id="tradeValue" placeholder="18000" min="0" inputmode="decimal" />
        </div>

        <div class="calc-field">
          <label for="cashToCover">Cash, Rebate, or Outside Help Used Against Negative Equity ($)</label>
          <input type="number" id="cashToCover" placeholder="3000" min="0" inputmode="decimal" />
        </div>

        <div class="calc-field">
          <label for="newCarPrice">New Vehicle Price Before Taxes and Fees ($)</label>
          <input type="number" id="newCarPrice" placeholder="36000" min="0" inputmode="decimal" />
        </div>

        <div class="calc-field">
          <label for="taxesFees">Taxes, Fees, Warranty, and Add-Ons ($)</label>
          <input type="number" id="taxesFees" placeholder="3500" min="0" inputmode="decimal" />
        </div>

        <div class="calc-field">
          <label for="downPayment">Down Payment on New Vehicle ($)</label>
          <input type="number" id="downPayment" placeholder="4000" min="0" inputmode="decimal" />
        </div>

        <div class="calc-field">
          <label for="apr">New Loan APR (%)</label>
          <input type="number" id="apr" placeholder="8.5" min="0" inputmode="decimal" />
        </div>

        <div class="calc-field">
          <label for="termMonths">New Loan Term (Months)</label>
          <input type="number" id="termMonths" placeholder="72" min="0" inputmode="numeric" />
